    "title": "Control Board 4e: slow never stops anything; Check and start again",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-19 (5:33 PM MST): a slow results endpoint (3.3 s against 0.2 s, three times) had tripped and stopped W1, and Resolve only asked What fixed it?: \"There is no way to fix this\" and \"no dead ends, system fixes first\". A slow call or job is now a warning that says how slow, stops nothing and clears itself when the speed returns. Slow trips already open are lifted by the system on the next watch: it checks first, then starts again what they stopped, and keeps trying while a check is red (logged, Undo for a day). Resolve is Check and start again, with no question, greyed with the reason while a check is red. A pre-flight line not tested in 6 hours is tested again by the watch, words only, so an old trip (W0) says what is really wrong. Replaces 3c's slow rule (decisions/0171 note).",
